      "title": "Head Coach Flag Football",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-24\n\nLocation: Crestview Hills\n\nAbout the Role: The Head Coach Flag Football position is a leadership role responsible for developing and managing a competitive and educational flag football program within an educational setting. The primary goal is to cultivate athletes' skills, teamwork, and sportsmanship while promoting physical fitness and a positive sporting environment. This role involves designing training sessions, strategizing game plans, and mentoring players to achieve both individual and team success. The Head Coach will also collaborate with school administrators, parents, and other coaches to ensure the program aligns with educational values and community standards. Ultimately, the position aims to foster a lifelong appreciation for sports and healthy competition among participants. Minimum Qualifications: Proven experience coaching flag football or a related sport at the youth or educational level. Strong knowledge of flag football rules, techniques, and strategies. Ability to communicate effectively with students, parents, and school staff. Background in physical education, sports management, or a related field is preferred. Certification in first aid and CPR or willingness to obtain upon hiring. Preferred Qualifications: Previous experience as a head coach or assistant coach in an educational or community sports program. Formal coaching certification from a recognized sports organization. Experience working with diverse student populations and fostering inclusive team environments. Knowledge of athlete development principles and injury prevention techniques. Demonstrated ability to organize and manage sports events or tournaments. Responsibilities: Plan, organize, and conduct regular flag football practices and training sessions tailored to various skill levels. Develop game strategies, analyze team performance, and make real-time decisions during competitions. Mentor and motivate student-athletes to improve their skills, teamwork, and sportsmanship. Coordinate with school officials, parents, and other stakeholders to support program goals and logistics. Ensure compliance with safety protocols, league rules, and educational policies related to student athletics. Skills: The Head Coach will utilize strong leadership and communication skills daily to inspire and guide athletes toward their full potential. Strategic thinking and analytical skills are essential for developing effective game plans and adapting tactics during competitions. Organizational skills are critical for managing practice schedules, coordinating with stakeholders, and ensuring compliance with safety and educational standards. The ability to teach and mentor young athletes fosters skill development and positive team dynamics. Additionally, interpersonal skills help build trust and collaboration among players, parents, and school personnel, creating a supportive and motivating environment.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=4f8993d7-7486-4f03-a125-59b813eb0331&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=498131519_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Public Safety Officer Part-Time",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-19\n\nLocation: Crestview Hills\n\nThomas More University is seeking dedicated Part-time Public Safety Officers to join our team and make a meaningful difference in the lives of our students and campus community.  Public Safety Officers serve as ambassadors of safety and hospitality by providing visible patrols, responding to emergencies, assisting community members, and helping create an environment where learning, faith, and service can flourish. If you are committed to serving others with professionalism, integrity, and respect, we encourage you to apply. About Us : Thomas More is an academic community in Northern Kentucky that provides a Catholic liberal arts education to men and women who are seeking to live lives of meaning.  As a Catholic diocsean university, Thomas More is university of the Diocese of Covington and as such is committed to the principles and beliefs that lay at the heart of Christianity, specifically those handed down by the Roman Catholic tradition. The university welcomes students and faculty of all faiths who have a desire to seek the Truth, do the Good, and love the Beautiful. Inspired by our three founding religious orders: the Benedictine Sisters, the Congregation of Divine Providence, and the Sisters of Notre Dame, our communal and academic life continues to faithfully follow the Catholic Intellectual Tradition.  As a university founded through three religious orders,  Thomas More University inherits a   treasured history from those charisms. Inspired by our founding orders, the university is guided by our Characteristics of a Saint : Hospitality, Humility, Service, and Stewardship . We strive to support a welcoming community that recognizes the dignity of every person, approaches learning and relationships with openness and humility, serves others with compassion and purpose, and faithfully stewards the gifts, opportunities, and responsibilities entrusted to us. These values shape our culture, inform our decisions, and inspire our commitment to educating our students to live lives of meaning in service of the common good.  As a liberal arts university, Thomas More University is committed to providing a liberal arts core of studies in the arts and sciences that is entirely informed by our engagement with the Catholic Intellectual Tradition. Devoted to the unity of faith and reason and the understanding that truth is one, the core seeks the integration of all disciplines. This integrative formation enables students to develop their capacity to discern the Truth, think critically, and engage in a sincere dialogue. The liberal arts foundation guides the career and professional paths students will take in the liberal arts, sciences, and business. Our students are invited to engage in a lifelog search for wisdom, not just information. Why Thomas More University? Commitment to Mission and Values : Thomas More University is guided by a mission that integrates faith and reason. Employees have the opportunity to contribute to a meaningful mission that emphasizes the holistic development of students in an inclusive, values-driven environment.  Supportive Community : Working on campus at Thomas More University means being part of a close-knit community that encourages collaboration, respect, and integrity. The university promotes a culture of support and professional growth.  Educational Benefits : Thomas More University offers tuition remission and other educational benefits for employees and their dependents, encouraging lifelong learning and development.  Competitive Benefits Package : Employees are offered a comprehensive benefits package, including health, dental, and retirement benefits. What You Will Do: Respond to service calls, including unlocking buildings, providing escorts, assisting motorists, and responding to suspicious activity or emergencies. Patrol the campus by vehicle, golf cart, or foot to ensure full coverage of campus buildings and grounds. Identify and report maintenance concerns and campus hazards to appropriate staff. Provide security at university functions and athletic events as needed. Administer basic first aid, CPR, and AED, coordinating with medical responders when necessary. Assist students in crisis, working with university staff and external resources to ensure proper care. Respond to campus security and fire alarms, ensuring appropriate action is taken. Maintain clear, timely daily logs and incident reports. Promote shared responsibility for campus safety and enforce university policies with tact and diplomacy. Perform duties in line with university policies, including the TMU Employee Manual. Work flexible hours to ensure 24/7 safety coverage. Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent required; additional education in criminal justice or related fields welcome. Excellent customer service, interpersonal, and communication skills, with the ability to handle stressful situations and diverse personalities. Knowledge of campus safety and security procedures, including fire/life safety and access control systems. Strong written and verbal communication skills, with proficiency in English grammar, spelling, and report writing. Ability to interpret and enforce university regulations with firmness and diplomacy. Good judgment, discretion, and the ability to analyze situations accurately and adopt effective courses of action. Ability to work independently, confidentially, and with minimal supervision. Proficiency in or ability to quickly learn new technologies relevant to safety systems and campus operations. Working Hours :  Public Safety provides 24/7 coverage. Shifts may vary based on operational needs, and the officer’s schedule will be determined by the Supervisor.  Physical Requirements:  Frequently: interact and communicate with university members and others. Frequently: extended periods of sitting, standing, walking, and operating a golf cart or motor vehicle. As necessary: climb stairs and run. Regularly: sit for desk-based tasks, perform fine manipulation, use a telephone/radio, write by hand, and sort/file paperwork. Regularly: kneel/crawl, twist, and lift/carry/push/pull objects weighing up to 35 pounds.",
      "department": ""
    },
